For the sake of reproducibility in research, I would like to refer readers/users to a specific version of INLA even after that version becomes outdated. I noticed that only the most recent few versions <http://www.math.ntnu.no/inla/R/stable/src/contrib/> are posted, and I'm worried that the current version will vanish within a few months of my next paper.

